add('B14', GB, 'D.J.: unknown tile that looks like katakana め', 'Unknown tile in the DJ minigame', [Rl(0x1A, 0x4000, 0xD80)], 'data', 'exact tile match of the TCRF picture (tools/dj_marker_tile.py)', 'LOCATED, pixel-exact (2026-10-19). The TCRF picture is a 5 x 6 pixel glyph (2x, 1 px margin). It equals EIGHT identical 8 x 8 tiles of the D.J. performer sheet 1A:4000-4D7F (the $D80 B that 05:438F copies to VRAM $8000): 1A:4360, 4460, 4490, 44D0, 4570, 45C0, 4740, 47F0 (sheet tile ids $36, $46, $49, $4D, $57, $5C, $74, $7F), bytes 00 00 44 44 24 24 1C 1C 18 18 34 34 60 60 00 00 (the glyph at (1,1) of the tile, colour 3 on colour 0; 13 hits in the JP ROM, the other 5 are the same tiles read one to two rows lower, not on a tile boundary). International ROM: the sheet is byte-identical to the JP sheet except 16 bytes: seven copies of the glyph at the same addresses, and at 1A:4740 (JP: the glyph) a different tile of the patterned run around it. Reading (owner, 2026-10-19): the glyph is a MARKER, a tile that shows a wrong tile reference; that reading is I (nothing in the code says so; no display check: the display tracker is value-matched and cannot tell the eight identical tiles apart).', 'C (location) / I (marker)', 'assets/unidentified/dj_marker_tile_sheet.png assets/unidentified/dj_marker_tile_hits.csv')
