add('B16', GB, 'Unused Graphic Bank 11: hand flipping through a newspaper', 'Completely unused graphic bank', [R(0x11, 0x5800, 0x693F)], 'data', 'bank views + exact cell search of the owner picture + OAM list $BA', "LOCATED (C: the owner's hint of 2026-10-13, confirmed as a yes on 2026-10-25, and the exact cell search): 11:5800-693F, label Unused_TCRF_HandNewspaperFrames_Gfx. Nine sprite frames of 25 tiles (5 x 5 sprites, 40 x 40 px) in 512-byte slots at 11:5800 + $200*j (j = 0-8, the last one cut at 11:693F), arranged by OAM list $BA of bank 01 (OamList_B01_4000_BA, 01:5504; tile T of frame j = ROM tile 11:5800+$200*j+16*(T-$50), attr $10). The owner's TCRF picture (341 x 193, 2x) is these frames with the tiles regrouped: every non-blank 8 x 8 cell of the nine frames is an exact tile of the span (cell search in the reduced picture, none unmatched), frames 0, 1, 3, 7, 8 equal the ROM render pixel for pixel, frames 5 and 6 within 3 and 2 px (overlap with the neighbour), frame 2 matches 827 of 851 px but the picture shows a sixth tile row above it, frame 4 is clipped at the right edge, matches in its top two tile rows, has a stray pixel column below them and lacks its bottom tile row in the picture. The 161-of-496 result of the first matcher (README 16.24) was for the picture taken from the PDF and is superseded. Coverage: the slots are read only in forced runs; no call that draws list $BA or loads these slots was found; the first 256 bytes before them (11:5700-57FF) are the second half of the main-menu frame loaded from 11:5600 and are on screen in normal play. Rendering from the ROM only: tcrf_check/tools/oam_frames_11_5800.py.", 'C', 'assets/unidentified/11_5800_frames_list_BA.png')
