add('B18', GB, 'R!R!R! star', '-', [Rl(0x1B, 0x6180, 0x20)], 'data', 'exact 8 x 16 block match (tools/run_star_pair.py) + BGB', 'LOCATED, pixel-exact (2026-10-19; replaces the one-tile candidate 1B:618A of the first matcher, which was the same star read ten bytes into the first tile). The TCRF picture (14 x 14 = 1 px margin + 6 x 6 at 2x) is the top-left 6 x 6 of a 7 x 7 star that straddles two tiles, so no single 8 x 8 tile holds it: it is the aligned tile pair 1B:6180 + 1B:6190 (rows 5-7 of the first, rows 0-3 of the second), the only such block in the ROM and in the international ROM, at the same address. The pair is OBJ id $B0 (8 x 16 sprites; VRAM $8B00; loaded with 1B:6100-667F by the race loader Mode21_State02_RaceSceneInit 09:614A). It is NOT unused: OAM list $1C of the table 02:6E4B (02:727F: sprites $B0 at y -8, $AE, $AC) is the first frame of the hurdle knocked-over animation (Run_DrawHurdles_Tbl6FB3 09:6FB3: 1C 02 1D 02 1E 02), drawn when the runner hits a hurdle: BGB (corpus entry 649 plus a fixed key stream, tools/bgb_run_star.py) requests list $1C 2 times after 30 presses and 6 times after 31, then lists $1D and $1E, and shows the star on the hurdle (assets/unidentified/run_star_hurdle_hit_bgb.png). The owner\'s earlier by-eye answer for 1B:618A is the same star.', 'C', 'assets/unidentified/run_star_pair.png assets/unidentified/run_star_pair_hits.csv assets/unidentified/run_star_hurdle_hit_bgb.png assets/unidentified/run_star_bgb_list_requests.csv')
