add('C12', GC, 'D.J. screen text (JP "TRIPY-H", "FEQ.")', 'Intl: TRIPPY-H, FRQ.', [Rl(0x1C, 0x78D0, 0x60), Rl(0x1D, 0x4500, 0x300), Rl(1, 0x6ED2, 25)], 'data', 'OAM list + tile render, BGB, both ROMs', 'LOCATED, drawn from the ROMs and seen in BGB (2026-10-19). "TRIPY-H" is not background: it is OAM list $A7 of the table 01:5D47 (JP: 01:6ED2, six 8 x 8 sprites, OBJ ids $47-$4C = tiles 1C:78D0-792F), requested with the tab sprites by DjEd_DrawPageTabs (05:46AD, the call at 05:46B8) on the SOUND I, SOUND II and NOISE pages. International ROM: list $A7 of its table 01:5D2B is at 01:6E9E and holds SEVEN sprites ($47-$4D, tiles 1C:78D0-793F), which is where the extra P of "TRIPPY-H" goes. "FEQ." is background: BG ids $76 and $77, map row 3, columns 15 and 16 of the page overlay 23:6B00 (SOUND I; 23:6900 for NOISE), tile data 1D:4500 + 16 x (id - $50) = 1D:4760 / 4770 (1D:4260 / 4270 on the NOISE page, which loads 1D:4000). The overlay maps are identical in both ROMs: only the tile 1D:4760 (and its copy 1D:4260) differs, rows 2-6 of it: "FE" in JP, "FR" in the international ROM; the tile 1D:4770 with the "Q." is the same. The SOUND I page was captured in BGB on the JP ROM (BG scroll SCX 0, SCY 252 reproduces the top 99 scan lines exactly with these tiles). Picture: assets/unidentified/dj_labels_jp_vs_intl.png (tools/dj_labels_jp_vs_intl.py).', 'C', 'assets/unidentified/dj_labels_jp_vs_intl.png assets/unidentified/dj_labels_jp_vs_intl.csv')
